    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass. The change is complete as a full-stack, additive implementation:\n\n**Change request:** *Every client needs an email. Do not let me save one without a proper email address.*\n\nEnforced at all three layers:\n\n1. **Front-end** (`features/clients/ClientsPage.tsx`) \u2014 added an `isValidEmail` check; on submit, a blank or malformed email surfaces `client-form-email-error` and the create mutation is not sent, so no `client-row-*` appears. A valid email clears the error and creates the row.\n\n2. **Server** (`ClientsPost.java`) \u2014 mirrors the same regex and throws before saving, so a request that bypasses the form writes neither a `client` row nor an audit record.\n\n3. **Database** (`V2__client_email_valid.sql`) \u2014 a new Flyway migration adds a `CHECK` constraint requiring a structurally valid, non-blank email, as the final backstop.\n\nTest results: 3/3 passing (blank rejected, malformed rejected, valid accepted). Front-end `typecheck` is clean, and all `data-testid` anchors the spec expects (`client-form-email`, `client-form-email-error`, `client-row-*`) are matched.",
